name: sim.packUInt8Table
description: Packs an array of uint8 numbers into a string
luaSynopsis: bytes data = sim.packUInt8Table(list uint8Numbers, int startUint8Index = 0, int uint8count = 0)
pythonSynopsis: buffer data = sim.packUInt8Table(int[] uint8Numbers, int startUint8Index = 0, int uint8count = 0)
inputs:
1. uint8Numbers: array containing uint8 numbers. Invalid byte number will be packed in an undefined manner.
2. startUint8Index: zero-based index from which on data should be packed. Can be omitted in which case 0 is used
3. uint8count: amount of uint8s that should be packed. Can be omitted in which case 0 is used (which indicates that the maximum available uint8s should be packed from the indicated startUint8Index)
outputs:
1. data: a buffer (values between 0 and 255) that contains the uint8 numbers
